                        @* Section 7 — MT4 vs MT5 *@
                        <div class="br-section" id="s7">
                            <h2 class="br-h2">7. MT4 vs MT5 — Key Differences Explained</h2>
                            <p class="br-p">MetaQuotes designed MT5 as the successor to MT4, but the two platforms are <strong>not backward compatible</strong> — MQL4 code does not run on MT5 and vice versa. This is why millions of traders still use MT4 despite MT5's technical advantages.</p>

                            <div class="br-highlights" style="border-color:#fed7aa;background:linear-gradient(135deg,#fff7ed,#fef3c7);">
                                <div class="br-highlights-title" style="color:#c2410c;"><i class="fa-solid fa-code me-2"></i>The MQL4 vs MQL5 Gap — Why MT4 Lives On</div>
                                <ul style="margin:0;padding:0 0 0 18px;line-height:2.2;font-size:14px;color:#374151;">
                                    <li>There are <strong>thousands of MQL4 EAs and indicators</strong> available for MT4 — many are free or low-cost</li>
                                    <li>MQL4 EAs cannot run on MT5 — conversion requires significant rewriting</li>
                                    <li>Many profitable strategies were coded in MQL4 and never ported</li>
                                    <li>Brokers that haven't upgraded keep MT4 traders locked in</li>
                                    <li>For new algorithmic projects, <strong>MQL5 is the better starting point</strong></li>
                                </ul>
                            </div>

                            <table class="br-facts-table" style="margin-top:20px;">
                                <thead>
                                    <tr>
                                        <th>Feature</th>
                                        <th style="text-align:center;color:#2563eb;">MT4</th>
                                        <th style="text-align:center;color:#16a34a;">MT5</th>
                                    </tr>
                                </thead>
                                <tbody>
                                    <tr><td>Timeframes</td><td style="text-align:center;">9</td><td style="text-align:center;color:#16a34a;font-weight:700;">21 ✓</td></tr>
                                    <tr><td>Pending Order Types</td><td style="text-align:center;">4</td><td style="text-align:center;color:#16a34a;font-weight:700;">6 ✓</td></tr>
                                    <tr><td>Strategy Tester</td><td style="text-align:center;">Single-threaded</td><td style="text-align:center;color:#16a34a;font-weight:700;">Multi-threaded ✓</td></tr>
                                    <tr><td>Asset classes</td><td style="text-align:center;">Forex, CFDs</td><td style="text-align:center;color:#16a34a;font-weight:700;">+ Stocks, Futures ✓</td></tr>
                                    <tr><td>Built-in indicators</td><td style="text-align:center;">30</td><td style="text-align:center;color:#16a34a;font-weight:700;">38 ✓</td></tr>
                                    <tr><td>Economic calendar</td><td style="text-align:center;color:#ef4444;">External only</td><td style="text-align:center;color:#16a34a;font-weight:700;">Built-in ✓</td></tr>
                                    <tr><td>EA library size</td><td style="text-align:center;color:#2563eb;font-weight:700;">Largest ✓</td><td style="text-align:center;">Growing</td></tr>
                                    <tr><td>Broker support</td><td style="text-align:center;color:#2563eb;font-weight:700;">Near-universal ✓</td><td style="text-align:center;">Wide but not all</td></tr>
                                </tbody>
                            </table>
                        </div>

                        <div class="br-divider"></div>

                        @* Section 8 — TradingView + Broker *@
                        <div class="br-section" id="s8">
                            <h2 class="br-h2">8. Using TradingView with Your Forex Broker</h2>
                            <p class="br-p">TradingView's broker integration lets you place and manage trades directly from the chart without switching to MT4/MT5. The integration is available for a growing number of brokers through TradingView's native Trading Panel.</p>

                            <div class="br-platform-grid" style="grid-template-columns:1fr;">
